<p align="center">
  <img src="assets/sonoma-wordmark.svg" alt="Sonoma Runtime" width="420">
</p>

<p align="center">An independent runtime for Xbox Series executables on Windows.</p>

---

Sonoma Runtime loads an Xbox Series (GDK) title executable on a Windows PC and runs it as an
ordinary process. It maps the title's PE images itself, provides the console-only system
libraries (kernel, memory, GDK runtime, audio, input, storage) on top of Windows, translates
the console's RDNA2 GPU programs directly into DXIL, and implements the console flavour of
Direct3D 12 on PC Direct3D 12. It is written from scratch in Rust, using only the standard
library.

## Status

This is a **proof of concept**. It is early, incomplete and slow, and nothing is playable.
Large parts of the platform are stubs or partial implementations, many GPU paths are
unoptimised, and most titles will stop long before their first frame.

What it has shown so far: one large retail title, supplied by its owner, was brought from
process start through its loading sequence to its front-end screens and main menu on a PC, at a
few frames per second. That is the extent of the claim.

